## Adversarial Review Summary

Latest completed rerun for the immediately previous local draft revision is recorded below for traceability.
This section has been refreshed after the current local patch wave so the remaining blocker list matches the draft that should be reviewed next.

| Provider | Verdict | Key findings |
|---|---|---|
| Claude | MAJOR | Approval-state drift still is not operationally mitigated on the real gate surfaces; the plan still lacks an explicit requirement to clear, supersede, or revision-bind the live GitHub `status:plan-approved` label and local `.planning/plan-approved/2460.md` marker for this draft lineage |
| Codex | MAJOR | Approval-state drift still targets the wrong surface (`docs/plans/README.md` row handling instead of the real approval gates), and the new harness-source evidence remains too directory-level and non-specific |
| Gemini | UNAVAILABLE | Provider attempt hit repeated `429 RESOURCE_EXHAUSTED / MODEL_CAPACITY_EXHAUSTED`; no substantive verdict was produced in r9 |

